WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.400
Happy New Year!

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.780
Might 2018 be the year

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:03.600
when the

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.640
Libertarian political party

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.520
finally

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.140
begins to make a real difference?

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.760
Many of us hoped last year's presidential race would be

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.140
the election where a Libertarian

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.960
finally broke through.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:18.880
But

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:19.880
that was

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.120
not to be.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.891
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.280
If you didn't get close

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.440
last election

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.480
with two candidates lots of people hated,

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.860
what's the point?

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:30.900
The point is, John

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.160
we did do well

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.620
in 2016.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.325
Nick Sarwark's the chairman

00:00:35.325 --> 00:00:36.840
of the Libertarian Party.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.400
We tripled all previous records

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.720
in the 45 year history of the Libertarian Party.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.500
We've never had that kind of support

00:00:43.506 --> 00:00:44.609
from the electorate.

00:00:44.609 --> 00:00:46.457
And that's great, tripled to what?

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.680
Four percent?

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.620
About three and a half.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.940
What's the point, if that's success?

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.080
Really, success is a long-term thing,

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:53.827
it's a process,

00:00:53.827 --> 00:00:55.880
it's not a particular election.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.060
More and more people are seeing

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.680
that when you elect Republicans,

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.948
you don't get this sort of small government they run on.

00:01:01.948 --> 00:01:03.316
If you elect Democrats,

00:01:03.316 --> 00:01:05.040
you don't get civil liberties,

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.260
you don't get any of the standing up for the little guy

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.820
that they say that they're all about.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.180
Both parties

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.939
are fighting over the ability to take your tax money

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.540
and give it to their corporate special-interest friends.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.580
And they're winning.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.666
Somehow their message

00:01:18.666 --> 00:01:20.860
is more compelling to more Americans.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.480
But we're growing and they're dying.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.080
Voter registration identity with

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.240
Republicans and Democrats is dropping.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.986
Voter registration identity with Libertarians

00:01:28.986 --> 00:01:30.500
is the only party that's growing.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:36.580
In a few years, the Libertarians will again hold

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.940
an open to everyone convention

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.660
to pick a nominee for the presidential race.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.180
Will that winner do

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:45.400
better than Gary Johnson did?

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.260
A lot of Libertarians say

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.780
it's Gary's fault.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.580
He was too low-key.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.500
He sounded like he was stoned.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.760
People aren't perfect.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.860
No one has the perfect combination of

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.280
credibility,

00:01:58.280 --> 00:01:59.240
experience,

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.820
purity of message.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.070
He was the best candidate

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.560
the delegates could have picked.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.500
And we had

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.280
the best success that we've ever had.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.920
Libertarians might have more success

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:08.560
if

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.680
Libertarian candidates were invited

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.680
to more of the TV debates.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.500
The parties filed a lawsuit to

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.440
try to force that to happen.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.740
The media tries to help the old party

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.920
politicians because it's simpler.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.360
It's simpler to run a story

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.480
where it's just Republicans and Democrats,

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.680
it's red and blue,

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.180
it's team A and team B.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.680
It's more complicated to say,

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.060
you know there are more political options out there.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.955
So they try and make us look silly.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.680
Gary Johnson looks silly on

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.080
MSNBC when he was

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.120
suddenly asked about Syria,

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.500
though he'd been talking about

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.640
domestic affairs.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.420
And I think the Republican Party

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.320
has gotten really extreme in that category.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.620
What would you do if you were elected

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.239
about Aleppo?

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:48.989
About?

00:02:48.989 --> 00:02:50.400
Aleppo?

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.060
And what is Aleppo?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.702
And he didn't know anything

00:02:53.702 --> 00:02:55.040
about where Aleppo is.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.800
He knew what Aleppo was.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:57.680
Absolutely,

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:58.760
and this is a common trick

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.980
in courtrooms and interviews everywhere

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.220
is you hit someone with a gotcha moment

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.460
and you take advantage of their confusion.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.680
It's a dirty trick,

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:07.528
but people pull it

00:03:07.528 --> 00:03:08.940
and that's what the media did.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.320
But now it's the new year,

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.340
another chance to show Americans

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.100
what Libertarians stand for.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.418
The rights of the individual,

00:03:18.418 --> 00:03:19.758
the right to free speech,

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.760
the right to keep and bear arms,

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.020
the limitations on the powers of government.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.273
Republicans and Democrats

00:03:25.273 --> 00:03:26.800
try to keep you off the ballot.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:27.780
Absolutely they do.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.000
They pass laws

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.000
specifically against Libertarians.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.580
In my home state of Arizona,

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.460
the Republicans passed a law

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.420
to increase our signature requirements

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.868
to get on the ballot

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:39.460
by up to thirty times.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:40.020
What do you mean,

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.480
specifically against Libertarians?

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:42.640
They can't do that.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.140
The floor debate in the legislature had

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.160
Republican leaders saying,

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.580
this is to stop Libertarian candidates

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.960
from running against us.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.800
We could lose our races if they run against us.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.620
They hate competition.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.760
And you're gonna be on the ballot in all 50 states?

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.020
That's the plan.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.360
They're already on the ballot in the yellow states.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.960
They're working on the gray states

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.900
Gary Johnson helped with that.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.040
He absolutely did.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.000
He brought a credibility to the party

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.320
and a popularity that we're building on now.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.480
But it's not about any particular candidate.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.800
That's the real difference between the Libertarian Party

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:17.750
and say,

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.060
Ross Perot.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.980
When Ross Perot gets tired of running for office,

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.920
there's nothing there anymore.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.400
The Libertarian Party

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.300
is millions of Americans

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.300
who have come together

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.400
and said

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.080
we want a right to live our life,

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.080
to pursue happiness any way we choose

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.540
as long as we don't hurt other people

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.380
and we don't take their stuff.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.860
And the two old political parties,

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.180
that's not what they're about.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:40.695
They're about taking power

00:04:40.695 --> 00:04:41.860
and controlling you.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:53.790
You

